.TH NVCM 1 "November 2026" "nvcm 1.0" "User commands"
.SH NAME
nvcm \- context-mixing compressor for text and source code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvcm
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B nvcm pack
< in > out
.br
.B nvcm unpack
< in > out
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dictionary compressors (xz, zstd) pay bits for a reference even when the
next character was completely predictable.
.B nvcm
instead predicts the next BIT with several models at once \(em byte
contexts of order 0\-8, a word model, and a match model \(em weighed
together by a mixer that learns which model tends to be right in this kind
of data, polished by two adaptive probability maps, and fed to a binary
arithmetic coder.
.PP
The price is speed: a few MB/s against zstd's hundreds.
.B nvz
therefore picks it only for blocks where it wins the probe, and only in
mode
.BR small .
On the Silesia and enwik8 corpora it beats \fBxz \-9e\fR
(1.677 and 1.713 bits/byte respectively, single-threaded).
.PP
The surface is gzip's:
.B \-d \-c \-k \-f \-t \-l \-v
mean what they mean there, the suffix is
.IR .nvcm ,
and with no file arguments the stream runs stdin to stdout.
.B \-1..\-9
are accepted and ignored \(em nvcm has no levels.
.PP
The worker subcommands
.BR pack / unpack
(aliases
.BR packa / packaupp )
are what
.B nvz
calls; they are listed here for completeness.
.SH MAGIC
Streams begin with NVCM1. The older magic NVZ01 is still read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 all well, 1 error, 2 refusal (broken stream, out of memory).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hz (1)
